{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/943736-dark-eras-what-are-you-guys-playing","id":943736,"title":"Dark Eras: What Are you Guys Playing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-04T11:22:25-07:00","id":943736,"title":"Dark Eras: What Are you Guys Playing?","content":"So, Dark Eras has been out for a while (at least for backers, but I think it's out already in POD, right?). So my question is, what are you guys doing with it? Running some games, which scenarios? etc?<br /> <br /> My group runs games in person and on a forum. So far, haven't started any in person, but we're doing two on the forums so far:<br /> <br /> Requiem for Regina: I love how the forum is great to go for a more literary feel and to describe the city of London in details. It helps to make the scenery feel very alive and for the players to fell immersed. Player's are an Invictus pirate, a Lancea et Sanctum plague survivor, a bon-vivant dramaturge in the Gallow's Post, a Lord Walsingham spy who doesn't know who embraced him and just joined the Sanctum and a 10-year old raised by animals who has some ties to the Cynn.<br /> <br /> Hunter Salem: In this game, we're trying something different. Each player has it's own topic, with only his point of view (and hidden from other players). While three of the five players have joined together already, the sense of dread and the unknown really plays well. Each player is with a conspiracy, but they're all playing safe so far. And they all have their own secrets to keep.<br /> <br /> We started the topic for Werewolf/Mage Neolithic, players are creating new characters, yet.<br /> <br /> Next the idea is to do a Musketeers Changeling game in the forums. As soon as Changeling Second Edition comes out. (Four is the limit of games we think it's doable to run on the forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Have not rum a game on the table and in person, mainly because most Second Editions are coming out right now. But we plan to do Viking Werewolf, Hunter Samurai and a crossover Aztec Empire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T14:03:57-07:00","id":949518,"title":"","content":"I'm playing the <i>glorious </i>Neolithic Mage.<br /> <br /> We're a Cabal of Mages who decided to play Civilization with our tribe, and unite the other tribes under one glorious banner.<br /> <br /> Or Storyteller is amused at our antics, because when he plays Exalted with us, we play slice of life and low-key adventure, but when he plays Chronicles of Darkness with us, we play Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T14:21:41-07:00","id":949530,"title":"","content":"My hypothetical Sundered World Mage aproves!","signature":"","edited":{"